From baee76b80a88a982aead3490242225aef754dc82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rigaz29 <ryanbagas27@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 16:41:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kernelsu: mark modules mounted on post-fs-data

backslashxx's ksud does not send EVENT_MODULE_MOUNTED after running
module scripts (upstream tiann does); it only exists as the manual
'ksud kernel notify-module-mounted' CLI. ksu_module_mounted therefore
stayed false forever, so ksu_handle_umount() bailed out early and apps
were never marked TIF_KSU_UNMOUNTABLE - breaking kernel_umount, the
sus_path/sus_map hiding and the sus_mount fdinfo/statfs spoofs.

By the time zygote forks apps, the module post-fs-data/post-mount
scripts have run, so set the flag on EVENT_POST_FS_DATA.
---
 drivers/kernelsu/supercall/dispatch.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/kernelsu/supercall/dispatch.c b/drivers/kernelsu/supercall/dispatch.c
index 5cadbd0ffa9..77e491480de 100644
--- a/drivers/kernelsu/supercall/dispatch.c
+++ b/drivers/kernelsu/supercall/dispatch.c
@@ -82,6 +82,16 @@ static int do_report_event(void __user *arg)
 			post_fs_data_lock = true;
 			pr_info("post-fs-data triggered\n");
 			on_post_fs_data();
+			// backslashxx ksud never sends EVENT_MODULE_MOUNTED on its
+			// own (upstream tiann does after running module scripts; here
+			// it only exists as the manual 'ksud kernel
+			// notify-module-mounted' CLI). Module post-fs-data/post-mount
+			// scripts have run by the time zygote forks apps, so mark
+			// modules mounted here to keep kernel_umount and the susfs
+			// umounted-app spoofs working.
+			ksu_module_mounted = true;
+			on_module_mounted();
+			pr_info("module mounted! (implied by post-fs-data)\n");
 		}
 		break;
 	}
